# tests/infra/run-all-classification.manifest — declared bucket for every
# tests/infra/test_*.sh (excl. test_helpers.sh, which run_all.sh's discovery
# excludes by name and is therefore never a row here).
#
# Format: `<test_basename> <bucket>` — one row per discovered test, comment
# lines (^\s*#) and blank lines ignored. Read via tests/infra/run-all-
# classification-lib.sh.  bucket is one of:
#
#   pool             — hermetic; safe to run concurrently in run_all.sh's
#                       host-global-bounded pool (H2).
#   intra-run-serial — mutates the invoking lane's own shared state (CoW
#                       target/, working-tree parser.c); must run serially
#                       WITHIN one run_all invocation, but different lanes'
#                       serial groups may still run concurrently with each
#                       other (isolated per-lane working trees).
#   host-exclusive   — does real CPU burn / real cgroup delegation / real
#                       reflink-FS + cargo; gives wrong answers or false-REDs
#                       under concurrent host load. Runs on the hot path
#                       (serially) while REIFY_RUN_ALL_EXCLUDE_HOST_INFRA=0
#                       (default); moves to the H9/Part-B cold lane once the
#                       knob flips to 1 (H3). See docs/prds/run-all-host-
#                       infra-partition.md §3 for the full rationale.
#
# Conservative-first, refine-later (PRD §3): the 4 host-exclusive entries
# below start whole-file host-exclusive as a conservative default; H5-H7
# refine them (moving hermetic portions into pool) by editing ONLY this
# manifest — the drift-guard (tests/infra/test_run_all_classification.sh)
# enforces the partition, not specific membership, so those reclassifications
# never need to touch the guard itself. Refinement is not strictly one-way:
# a pool rescue that fails to converge under real host load gets reclassified
# BACK to host-exclusive (task #4997 reversed H5's cpu_load_governance
# pool-rescue on exactly this basis) — see the PRD's "Superseded by #4997"
# notes.
#
# This file, the accessor lib, and the guard are LOAD-BEARING verify-pipeline
# artifacts (see scripts/verify-pipeline-infra-tests.txt) — an edit here
# routes the task through the full --scope all gate (see CLAUDE.md /
# scripts/verify-pipeline-guard.sh).
#
# Keystone for H2 (reads intra-run-serial), H3/H9 (read host-exclusive), and
# H5-H7 (reclassify entries as they rescue/split host-exclusive files).

# --- intra-run-serial (3) ----------------------------------------------------
test_reify_audit_ptodo.sh intra-run-serial
test_tree_sitter_pipeline.sh intra-run-serial
test_verify_semaphore_e2e.sh intra-run-serial

# --- host-exclusive (4) ------------------------------------------------------
test_cpu_governed_exec_hostexcl.sh host-exclusive
test_cpu_load_governance.sh host-exclusive
test_cpu_load_governance_deflake.sh host-exclusive
test_warm_lane_pool.sh host-exclusive

